        {
          "text": "The guide is scrutinizing one specimen while directing the participants' attention toward several mushrooms growing nearby.",
          "grammar": "while＋現在分詞",
          "ja": "ガイドは1つの標本を詳しく調べながら、近くに生えている複数のキノコへ参加者の注意を向けています。",
          "type": "detail",
          "points": 40
        },
        {
          "text": "The contrasting cap colors, spots, stems, and sizes provide visible morphological features that can be compared during identification.",
          "grammar": "関係代名詞that / 受動態",
          "ja": "傘の色、斑点、柄、大きさの違いは、識別時に比較できる目に見える形態的特徴となっています。",
          "type": "detail",
          "points": 40
        },
        {
          "text": "Accurate identification is essential because edible and toxic mushrooms may occasionally share deceptively similar characteristics.",
          "grammar": "because / may",
          "ja": "食用のキノコと有毒なキノコが紛らわしいほど似た特徴を持つ場合があるため、正確な識別が不可欠です。",
          "type": "inference",
          "points": 40
        },
        {
          "text": "The surrounding moss, leaf litter, and trees may also provide clues about the habitat in which particular species occur.",
          "grammar": "may / 関係詞in which",
          "ja": "周囲の苔、落ち葉、木々も、特定の種類が生育する環境を判断する手掛かりになる可能性があります。",
          "type": "inference",
          "points": 40
        },
        {
          "text": "Responsible foraging requires more than simply judging whether a mushroom appears visually palatable.",
          "grammar": "require more than / whether節",
          "ja": "責任ある採集には、キノコが見た目に食べられそうかどうかを判断する以上の知識が必要です。",
          "type": "inference",
          "points": 40
